---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Job Placement
description: Hands-on support from resume to signed offer — matching, coaching, and negotiation help for candidates who want a job placed, not just applications sent.
glass: true
extraScripts:
  - /assets/js/count-up.js
  - /assets/js/faq-accordion.js
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}

{# ================================================================
   JOB PLACEMENT — pilot redesign (Hallmark audit pass).

   This page is the test case for pulling the site's stronger AI tells out of one
   template before deciding whether to roll the same changes across the sibling
   service pages. Changes made here and NOT yet elsewhere:

   · Hero drops the aurora-blob + dot-field background — solid paper ground, the
     glass photo panel and the floating $0 tag carry the depth on their own.
   · Section heads are single-column: label (where it earns one) sits directly
     above its heading in the same column. No more tag-left / heading-right grid,
     no chapter-marker ghost index, no eyebrow on sections that aren't ordinal.
   · "What's included" is a definition list with inline icons on hairline rules,
     not a six-up grid of glass cards with stacked icon chips.
   · Fabricated proof is gated: the success story, the candidate-quote grid, and
     the employer logo wall are commented out until real, consented content exists.
     See the TODO markers below.
   ================================================================ #}

{% set crumbs = [{ label: "Home", url: "/" }, { label: "Services", url: "/services/" }, { label: "Job Placement" }] %}

{# ---------- Hero ----------
   Answers the fee question in the first screen (PRD §4) as a floating tag on the
   photograph, not small print under the buttons. ---------- #}
<section class="relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="section-container pb-14 pt-8 sm:pb-20 sm:pt-12">
    {% include "partials/breadcrumb.njk" %}

    <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        <p class="eyebrow">A named recruiter, start to finish</p>

        <h1 class="mt-4 font-grotesk text-4xl font-bold leading-[1.05] tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-6xl">
          Get placed, not just applied.
        </h1>
        <p class="lead-copy mt-5 max-w-xl">
          A named recruiter works your search end to end — resume, matching,
          interview prep, and negotiation — because a job search shouldn't be
          something you do alone.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row">
          <a href="{{ '/contact/' | url }}" class="btn-primary">
            {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }} Start your job search
          </a>
          <a href="{{ '/services/' | url }}" class="btn-outline">
            See all services
          </a>
        </div>

        {# TODO: confirm these figures with the client before launch — see stats.json.
           Candidate-facing, so lead with the success rate, not the partner count. #}
        {% set heroStats = [] %}
        {% for s in stats.list %}
          {% if s.label != "Partner Companies" %}{% set _ = heroStats.push(s) %}{% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
        <dl class="mt-10 grid max-w-lg grid-cols-3 gap-4 border-t border-ink/10 pt-6">
          {% for stat in heroStats.slice(0, 3) %}
          <div>
            <dd class="stat-figure text-xl sm:text-2xl"
                data-count-up data-target="{{ stat.value }}" data-suffix="{{ stat.suffix }}">0{{ stat.suffix }}</dd>
            <dt class="stat-label">{{ stat.label }}</dt>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class="relative lg:col-span-5">
        {% set coverImage = images.services["job-placement"].cover %}
        <div class="glass-panel p-3">
          <img src="{{ coverImage.url }}"
               alt="{{ coverImage.alt }}"
               width="1400" height="1750" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"
               class="aspect-[4/5] w-full rounded-[1.1rem] object-cover">
        </div>

        {# Frost, not pane — it floats over the photograph. See THEME.md §3. #}
        <div class="glass-frost absolute -bottom-4 left-6 rounded-2xl px-5 py-3.5 sm:-left-6">
          <p class="meta">Cost to you</p>
          <p class="font-grotesk text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">$0</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# TODO — Employer wall gated. `placed-at.njk` hotlinks logo.clearbit.com for
   Amazon / Microsoft / Accenture etc., which reads as a client list we can't
   substantiate. Re-enable only with a real, permitted set of employer names.
{% include "partials/placed-at.njk" %}
#}

{# ---------- What's included ---------- #}
<section id="included" class="section-container scroll-mt-28 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="section-title">Six things you get, from day one.</h2>
    <p class="lead-copy mt-4">Support at every stage of the search, not just a stack of applications sent on your behalf.</p>
  </div>

  {% set included = [
    { icon: "check", t: "Resume & profile optimization", d: "We rebuild your resume and profile around what actually gets noticed." },
    { icon: "users", t: "Interview coaching", d: "Mock interviews and real feedback before it counts." },
    { icon: "target", t: "Employer matching", d: "We only put you in front of roles that fit your background and goals." },
    { icon: "chart", t: "Offer negotiation support", d: "We help you evaluate and negotiate before you sign anything." },
    { icon: "clock", t: "Post-placement check-in", d: "We follow up at 30 and 90 days to make sure it's working out." },
    { icon: "briefcase", t: "Application tracking", d: "One recruiter, one thread — no chasing status across job boards." }
  ] %}
  <dl class="mt-10 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-7 sm:grid-cols-2">
    {% for item in included %}
    <div class="flex gap-4 border-t border-ink/15 pt-5">
      <span class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-brand">{{ icon(item.icon, "w-5 h-5") }}</span>
      <div>
        <dt class="card-title">{{ item.t }}</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1.5 body-copy">{{ item.d }}</dd>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </dl>

  {# We state our position on a placement that doesn't work out plainly, rather
     than leaving it to the FAQ. #}
  <p class="mt-10 file-inset meta max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
    No guarantee of an offer, and no promise on timeline — but if a placement
    doesn't work out inside 90 days, we re-open your search at no additional cost.
  </p>
</section>

{# ---------- What changes ----------
   Qualitative only, per PRD §4 — no salary figures, no timelines. The assertion
   does the work of a heading and a lead paragraph in one line. ---------- #}
<section id="changes" class="scroll-mt-28 border-y border-white/60 bg-paper/50 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="assertion sm:text-3xl">
        On your own, an application goes into a void. With us, it goes to
        someone already expecting it.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="ledger min-w-[34rem]">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">On your own</th>
            <th scope="col">With us</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% set contrasts = [
            { a: "Applications into a void, no reply", b: "A named recruiter who tells you where each one stands" },
            { a: "No idea why you were passed over", b: "Feedback after every interview" },
            { a: "Competing with hundreds of applicants", b: "Introduced to employers already expecting your resume" },
            { a: "Guessing what the interview will cover", b: "Prepped for the specific team you're meeting" }
          ] %}
          {% for row in contrasts %}
          <tr>
            <td class="w-1/2 pr-6">{{ row.a }}</td>
            <td class="w-1/2 font-medium text-ink">{{ row.b }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- The process ----------
   Genuinely ordinal, so it keeps step numbers — supplied by process-timeline.njk. #}
<section id="procedure" class="section-container scroll-mt-28 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <p class="eyebrow">Step by step</p>
    <h2 class="section-title mt-2">Five steps to an offer.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10">
    {% set steps = [
      { label: "Consultation", duration: "30 minutes", description: "A conversation about where you are and where you want to go." },
      { label: "Profile build", duration: "3–5 days", description: "Resume, profile, and positioning built around your target roles." },
      { label: "Matching", duration: "Ongoing", description: "Introductions only to employers that fit — no mass applications." },
      { label: "Interviews", description: "Coaching before every conversation that matters." },
      { label: "Offer", description: "Negotiation support and a check-in once you've started." }
    ] %}
    {% include "partials/process-timeline.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>

